C.2 Finding and scheduling the six participants
The CEO will prepare a list of potential participants from people we have already met: students living in the hostels, canteen owners or managers, cashiers and kitchen staff. We should aim to include at least one owner or manager, one cashier or kitchen staff member and three or more students. Each session will take around 40–45 minutes. The CTO will lead at least three sessions and make sure a DEMO-mode canteen is ready before each one.

C.3 How we will run each session
Before the session: Give the participant an ID and explain why we are speaking with them, how we will take notes and how their feedback may be used. Record audio only with their permission, and do not use their name publicly without consent. One founder asks the questions while the other records the participant's exact words. Agree on the three things we most want to learn before starting.
Warm-up (5 min): who they are, their role.
Past behaviour (15–20 min): the role-specific questions in ceo-submission.md E.2.
Prototype observation (10–15 min): tasks, not instructions; think aloud; no help for 30 seconds when stuck (cto-submission.md I.2).
Money and commitment (5 min): current spend first, then one concrete offer, then a commitment request.
After the session (within 24 hours): Complete the session record and hesitation log, share the three main takeaways with the other founder and update the register if the feedback changes our priorities.

