D. Venture metrics
The panel asked us to choose a meaningful venture metric. Our current proposal is the number of students who place repeat orders in a week. Both founders still need to confirm this choice (see decision D-09).

D.1 Primary metric — weekly repeat-ordering students
Definition: students who collected two or more app orders in the same calendar week.
Formula: repeat rate = students with ≥ 2 collected app orders in the week ÷ students with ≥ 1 collected app order in the week.
Sign-ups tell us that someone was curious enough to try SERVE. Repeat orders give us a better indication of whether the product is useful enough for them to return.
Data source: the Order table (status, channel, studentId, createdAt).
Frequency: weekly, reviewed at the weekly sync.
This metric will become useful only after a pilot with real students begins. Early numbers may be small and can fluctuate. It also cannot explain why someone stopped ordering, and promotions or canteen closures may affect the result.
The CEO can use this metric to understand whether students are returning and whether the product may have value worth paying for. The CTO can investigate whether a drop is linked to usability or reliability by checking the relevant logs.
The following read-only query is intended for the pilot database. The CTO checked the table and column names against backend/prisma/schema.prisma and tested the query against the test database.

SELECT week,
       count(*) FILTER (WHERE orders >= 2) AS repeat_students,
       count(*)                            AS active_students
FROM (
  SELECT "studentId", date_trunc('week', "createdAt") AS week, count(*) AS orders
  FROM "Order"
  WHERE status = 'COLLECTED' AND channel = 'APP'
  GROUP BY "studentId", date_trunc('week', "createdAt")
) per_student_week
GROUP BY week
ORDER BY week;
