E.2 AI in the product and in our work
We reviewed the backend, all three apps and the shared packages. Based on that code review, SERVE does not currently make calls to an AI service. That means there is no AI service cost per user and no AI-service dependency in the running product. If we add Market Intelligence or another AI feature later, we will record its cost per call and the effect of a service failure here.

We have used AI tools while building SERVE and preparing some of the documentation. We want to be transparent about that. These are the checks we expect to follow:

Code: The CTO must review and understand AI-assisted code. It must pass npm run typecheck, npm run lint and the relevant test suites, and be reviewed through a pull request.
Research: We will open and check the original source for every factual claim used in the pitch.
Content: We will never use AI-generated quotes, numbers or user findings. Quotes must come from session records, and numbers must come from actual measurements, bills or other recorded evidence.
Documents: Both founders will review a document before it is committed or shared. Anything we have not verified will be marked TO BE CONFIRMED.
Costs: The CEO will include any paid AI tools in the cost register using the actual plan or subscription cost. We still need to supply those figures.

