I. Preparing for the swapped demo
I.1 Before we start
PostgreSQL running; backend started; /api/health/db reports ok.
Staff (5173), admin (5174) and student (5555) apps open, each in its own browser profile (all apps share one sign-in cookie on localhost).
Database migrated and seeded; an admin created with npm run admin:create --workspace backend.
A Google OAuth client configured on the demo machine (otherwise explain student sign-in instead of showing it).
The demo canteen in DEMO payment mode and taking orders.
A staff account approved for that canteen with Cashier granted.
One full rehearsal on the demo machine on the same day.

I.2 Demo flow (around 8 minutes)
Start with the architecture in one sentence: three apps, one backend and one database.
Student signs in and opens the menu.
Student places an order; the server sets the price.
Student pays the DEMO QR and taps I've paid.
Cashier confirms with Simulate payment received; the order appears on the kitchen board.
Kitchen moves it to Preparing and Ready; the student screen updates live.
Pause orders; the student cannot order; Resume orders.
Collected.
Admin report.
Be clear about the current limits: payments are simulated and no real money moves; wait-time estimates are not available; pausing is manual; and there is no pickup code. Real payments, fixing the mock-payment shortcut and deployment are production tasks for the future.

